    <node id="Chain-Of-Thought (Cot)">
      <data key="d0">Chain-Of-Thought (Cot)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chain-of-Thought (CoT) is a method of providing correct but possibly systematically different solutions for tasks such as math problems or program execution traces.&lt;SEP&gt;Chain-of-Thought (CoT) is a process used in unified multi-modal understanding/generative models to incorporate fine-grained understanding into image editing performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Chain-of-thought refers to the intermediate reasoning process in a model's generation of answers.&lt;SEP&gt;Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting has emerged as a simple and effective way to elicit step-by-step solutions from large language models (LLMs).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad3ff5a016386baadd7feb243f306901&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2643db96ff06ade733f1ed549959310e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb47cac146c7b2f3ef3d164ff921698&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e65899f92452776d1e2d8e56956888d2</data>
