    <node id="Large Language Model (LLM)">
      <data key="d0">Large Language Model (LLM)</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">**Large Language Model (LLM)**

The Large Language Model, also known as LLM, is a type of artificial intelligence used in various applications. It is primarily employed for scoring clinician-preferred outputs higher than rejected ones, indicating its ability to evaluate and improve the quality of generated text.

In addition to its use in evaluating AI-generated content, the LLM has been utilized in analyzing 5,300 reports from documented AI incidents. This highlights its potential as a tool for understanding and mitigating the risks associated with artificial intelligence.

Large Language Models are increasingly being deployed in high-stakes and operational settings, which necessitates the development of evaluation strategies that go beyond aggregate accuracy. These models require more nuanced approaches to assess their performance and effectiveness.

The LLM is also used in A2DEPT for system-level algorithmic expressiveness and open-ended generation. This suggests its potential applications in areas such as natural language processing and text generation.

An empirical study on large language models revealed model-dependent refinement quality and safety lessons, underscoring the importance of understanding the specific characteristics and limitations of these models.

Furthermore, the LLM is a type of deep learning model used in natural language processing tasks. Its architecture and design enable it to process and generate human-like text with a high degree of accuracy.

In existing multi-agent code generation frameworks, the Large Language Model is used for execution feedback and iterative improvement. This highlights its potential as a tool for improving the performance and efficiency of AI systems.

Overall, the Large Language Model is a sophisticated artificial intelligence model designed to process and generate human-like text. Its applications are diverse, ranging from evaluating AI-generated content to improving the performance of multi-agent code generation frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;LLM is a type of model used for re-ranking and achieving superior performance, but it is computationally prohibitive and prone to noise inherent in perplexity estimation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Large Language Model is a type of model that benefits from the proposed data valuation framework.&lt;SEP&gt;The Large Language Model is a type of deep learning model used for various natural language processing tasks, including information retrieval and ranking effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Large Language Models are a type of deep learning model that can achieve strong performance in various tasks, including CSP.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0d551161566faf30fdc24dbde48ebfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-381164f8e5eeb1538b53d25d3cf781b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddabb643ad7982794978859b96daf403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-626cc6bade27470185f730dbb83ee93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d0cda25c660336dba17f393f96c07ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4675567f8736cc58a7d6d63b7a67f3c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e559bc1a568b70c4f4f5ba308022bb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e362b1abd07592b478809f67c6a95bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1194bf14d2da400395521fd4c013e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45150d1184b48644574f184fced8240b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d6e4ada5453c7cde973c876f445327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d92623b24805aae743314ad5136c703</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24710v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.24519v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.24076v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.24043v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23523v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23505v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23106v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.22971v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.22722v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.22893v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.22180v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.21957v1</data>
