    <node id="Minecraft">
      <data key="d0">Minecraft</data>
      <data key="d1">application</data>
      <data key="d2">Minecraft is a video game used as a benchmark to evaluate agents' capacity in the discovery-to-application loop.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7909c6cfbc42d7e40e309323a850e887</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24697v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780258507</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Scicrafter">
      <data key="d0">Scicrafter</data>
      <data key="d1">benchmark</data>
      <data key="d2">SciCrafter is a Minecraft-based benchmark that operationalizes the discovery-to-application loop through parameterized redstone circuit tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7909c6cfbc42d7e40e309323a850e887</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24697v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780258507</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Discovery-To-Application Loop">
      <data key="d0">Discovery-To-Application Loop</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The discovery-to-application loop refers to the process of discovering causal regularities and applying them to build functional systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7909c6cfbc42d7e40e309323a850e887</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24697v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780258512</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Agent Viability Framework">
      <data key="d0">Agent Viability Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">framework</data>
      <data key="d2">The Agent Viability Framework establishes three properties (monitoring, anticipation, and monotonic restriction) as individually necessary and collectively sufficient for documented failure modes in AI agents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c127bc04f3bde0cd314a75a26f2cec3</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24686v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780258830</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Aubin'S Viability Theory">
      <data key="d0">Aubin'S Viability Theory</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Aubin's viability theory provides the theoretical foundation for the Agent Viability Framework, establishing conditions for AI agent safety and viability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c127bc04f3bde0cd314a75a26f2cec3</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24686v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780258830</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Autopilot">
      <data key="d0">Autopilot</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">The Autopilot is a closed-loop system formalised as an instance of Aubin's regulation map with kill-switch-as-last-resort, used in RiskGate to ensure AI agent safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c127bc04f3bde0cd314a75a26f2cec3</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24686v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780258837</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Informational Viability Principle">
      <data key="d0">Informational Viability Principle</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Informational Viability Principle proposes governing an AI agent by estimating a bound on unobserved risk and allowing actions when their capacity exceeds the estimated bound by a safety margin.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c127bc04f3bde0cd314a75a26f2cec3</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24686v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780258837</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Riskgate">
      <data key="d0">Riskgate</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">RiskGate instantiates the Agent Viability Framework with dedicated statistical estimators, a fail-secure monotonic pipeline, and a closed-loop Autopilot formalised as an instance of Aubin's regulation map with kill-switch-as-last-resort.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c127bc04f3bde0cd314a75a26f2cec3</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24686v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780258841</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Viability Index">
      <data key="d0">Viability Index</data>
      <data key="d1">metric</data>
      <data key="d2">The Viability Index $VI(t) \in [-1,+1]$ is a scalar metric that predicts the viability of an AI agent at time $t$ and transforms governance from reactive to predictive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c127bc04f3bde0cd314a75a26f2cec3</data>
