    <node id="Humans">
      <data key="d0">Humans</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Humans are participants in the study who demonstrate a robust trust effect in their use of Turkish evidential morphology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c55766a45b0f180acb4d559b875dcdd9</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24665v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780259787</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Source Trustworthiness">
      <data key="d0">Source Trustworthiness</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Source trustworthiness refers to the perceived reliability or credibility of a source, which can influence the use of evidential morphology in Turkish.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c55766a45b0f180acb4d559b875dcdd9</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24665v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780259794</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Turkish Evidential Morphology">
      <data key="d0">Turkish Evidential Morphology</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Turkish evidential morphology refers to the use of suffixes in Turkish to indicate the reliability or trustworthiness of a source.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c55766a45b0f180acb4d559b875dcdd9</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24665v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780259798</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dysib">
      <data key="d0">Dysib</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">DySIB is a method for learning low-dimensional representations of time-series data by maximizing predictive mutual information between past and future observation windows while penalizing representation complexity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8bcf22c0d460fde620c812a0c96baa6f</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24662v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780259999</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Experimental Video Dataset">
      <data key="d0">Experimental Video Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The dataset consists of video recordings of a physical pendulum, which are used to evaluate the performance of DySIB.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8bcf22c0d460fde620c812a0c96baa6f</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24662v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780259999</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Latent Space">
      <data key="d0">Latent Space</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The latent space refers to the low-dimensional representation of time-series data learned by DySIB, which operates entirely in this space and avoids reconstruction of the observations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8bcf22c0d460fde620c812a0c96baa6f</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24662v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780260006</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Physical Pendulum">
      <data key="d0">Physical Pendulum</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The physical pendulum is an experimental system used to demonstrate the effectiveness of DySIB in recovering interpretable dynamical coordinates directly from high-dimensional data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8bcf22c0d460fde620c812a0c96baa6f</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24662v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780260006</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Predictive Mutual Information">
      <data key="d0">Predictive Mutual Information</data>
      <data key="d1">metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Predictive mutual information is a measure used in DySIB to maximize the predictive power of the learned representations while penalizing representation complexity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8bcf22c0d460fde620c812a0c96baa6f</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24662v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780260010</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Phase Space">
      <data key="d0">Phase Space</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The phase space refers to the low-dimensional representation of a physical system's dynamics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8bcf22c0d460fde620c812a0c96baa6f</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24662v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780260010</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Agentward Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Agentward Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">architecture</data>
      <data key="d2">The AgentWard architecture integrates stage-specific, heterogeneous controls with cross-layer coordination to intercept threats along their propagation paths while safeguarding critical assets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d66caa329c3a04aee4985803a47142b6</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24657v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780260217</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Autonomous AI Agents">
      <data key="d0">Autonomous AI Agents</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Autonomous AI agents extend large language models into full runtime systems, loading skills, ingesting external content, maintaining memory, planning multi-step actions, and invoking privileged tools.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d66caa329c3a04aee4985803a47142b6</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24657v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780260217</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Openclaw">
      <data key="d0">Openclaw</data>
      <data key="d1">application</data>
      <data key="d2">OpenClaw is a plugin-native platform used for implementing and demonstrating the practical feasibility of the AgentWard architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;OpenClaw is an AI agent framework enabling skill-augmented AI agents for complex biomedical workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;OpenClaw is an autonomous agent system introducing significant efficiency challenges due to long-context inputs and multi-turn reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d66caa329c3a04aee4985803a47142b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05877db4970d1baba025bbf14edc0989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9fadbd7a582ff38d14441fdbe880d8a</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24657v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23674v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.22577v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780375313</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lifecycle Security Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Lifecycle Security Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">architecture</data>
      <data key="d2">A lifecycle security architecture that systematically organizes protection across five stages of autonomous AI agents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d66caa329c3a04aee4985803a47142b6</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24657v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780260229</data>
