    <node id="Mnist">
      <data key="d0">Mnist</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">MNIST is a dataset used in the continual-learning benchmarks, which includes handwritten digits.&lt;SEP&gt;MNIST is a dataset used to evaluate the performance of models trained using Learn&amp;Drop's method.&lt;SEP&gt;MNIST is another dataset used for evaluating the performance of activation functions, with E-GEM achieving the best result (99.23%).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-899149a6310f6cac289e14d7be815549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e271b74806dc276d5174bade6921f998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f9d8ef8dcee4b84c3e9529d0d4d52a</data>
