    <node id="Vision-Language Models">
      <data key="d0">Vision-Language Models</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">**Vision-Language Models**

Vision-Language Models (VLMs) are advanced models that integrate computer vision and natural language processing to enable joint reasoning over text and images. They have demonstrated strong performance on textbook-style physics problems but frequently fail in dynamic real-world scenarios due to an over-reliance on linguistic priors, which can lead to object hallucination.

Despite these limitations, VLMs are increasingly used as evaluators in tasks requiring nuanced image understanding, yet their reliability remains underexplored. They have been proposed as general-purpose tools for scientific data interpretation and benefit from Reinforcement Learning for enhanced reasoning. However, like Large Language Models (LLMs), they struggle with interactive causal learning and transferring latent structures across contexts.

VLMs are a type of deep learning architecture that can be brittle when used for end-to-end prompting, but they have been successfully applied in various applications, including wellbeing assessment. Their performance is often undermined by object hallucination due to an over-reliance on linguistic priors, which highlights the need for further research into their reliability and robustness.

Overall, Vision-Language Models are a powerful tool for integrating computer vision and natural language processing, but they require careful consideration of their limitations and potential biases in order to be effectively utilized.&lt;SEP&gt;Vision-Language Models is mentioned in a relation extracted from the chunk.&lt;SEP&gt;VLM stands for Vision-Language Model, which can recognize what happens in video but struggles with counting how many times an action occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Vision-Language Model is used to encode schematics and descriptions in AnalogRetriever.&lt;SEP&gt;Vision-language models are used to produce short textual rationales for diabetic retinopathy grading.&lt;SEP&gt;Vision-language models are a type of AI model that combines computer vision and natural language processing to perform various tasks, including image classification and object detection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ac408a983efd5ccb658b88f8bdc1379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fae825413dbd09250459cbd5bbfe30c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b83f3702bd088008cc6feaedfe42bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f986b39741d6de97b65a3c203f1521e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6a8292ee988e4d64c218b75e3c5f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a01dcb477b76a4cacbd754ce4561d7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c498a8ef8a91dd7345a0bc0c56faeed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da21e03ceeb42171cedd9a558d6bcf3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26dafa661cb0d231f43ed8c9672433fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-201c68b063975a5b0441ceab4c211673&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24290bb35376401e34d3a4168d44a3d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-944fe7c5b62b63d7ff6de501644a34a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f633f2dba8bf8f7b632c997bdbf3ace</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24589v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.24443v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.24396v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.24346v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.24339v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.24179v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.24062v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23786v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23724v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23407v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23195v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23079v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.21346v1</data>
