    <node id="Lora">
      <data key="d0">Lora</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation) is another capability carrier that can be used within the Diffusion Templates framework.&lt;SEP&gt;LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation) is a technique that adapts the model's weights by reducing their rank, which can help improve the model's performance on sequential tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;LoRA is a widely adopted method for parameter-efficient fine-tuning, requiring lower ranks than vector-based adaptation methods but offering competitive performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f36584a3c17d75781a357f1a3e17848d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-350265fa6cfa6c36f900b8cfb64b92be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72f506dc6a19884a69d054a9c34679</data>
