    <node id="Reinforcement Learning (Rl)">
      <data key="d0">Reinforcement Learning (Rl)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Reinforcement Learning is a method used to enhance the reasoning ability of VLMs.&lt;SEP&gt;Reinforcement Learning is a classical method used in AI that fails catastrophically when attempting to induce latent structures through sequential exploration and transfer them across contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;RL is a machine learning paradigm used to train MLLM agents on dynamic GUI tasks by interacting with the environment and receiving rewards or penalties.&lt;SEP&gt;Reinforcement Learning (Rl) is mentioned in a relation extracted from the chunk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee6a8292ee988e4d64c218b75e3c5f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c498a8ef8a91dd7345a0bc0c56faeed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8227fa84b33ba6c4091b7e5804332bdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44784699c64a5aec415cf1e1bb031fa</data>
