    <node id="Reinforcement Learning">
      <data key="d0">Reinforcement Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">**Reinforcement Learning**

Reinforcement learning is a type of machine learning that involves training agents through rewards or penalties for their actions. This approach is particularly useful in situations where the goal is to optimize a specific outcome, such as maximizing profits or minimizing costs. In the context of autonomous decision-making, reinforcement learning enables agents to learn from their environment and adapt their behavior accordingly.

Reinforcement learning has been applied in various domains, including automated dispatching rules, where it can help improve scalability by reducing the complexity of graph-based models. However, existing implementations often struggle with quadratic graph complexity or architectural overhead due to heterogeneous layers. To address these challenges, researchers have proposed innovative solutions, such as EPM-RL, which distills high-cost agentic reasoning into a trainable in-house model.

Reinforcement learning is also used to formalize model and feedback uncertainty via counterfactual logic. This approach enables the development of more robust and reliable decision-making systems by accounting for potential uncertainties and ambiguities. Furthermore, reinforcement learning has been inspired by other ideas, such as HPO (Hyperparameter Optimization), which draws upon its principles to generate training signals using information unavailable during execution.

In addition to its applications in autonomous decision-making, reinforcement learning is also used to fine-tune ASR (Automatic Speech Recognition) models after initial training with supervised bootstrapping. This approach can help improve the accuracy and efficiency of speech recognition systems by adapting them to specific environments or tasks.

Overall, reinforcement learning is a powerful tool for training agents to make decisions based on rewards or penalties. Its applications span various domains, from automated dispatching rules to ASR model fine-tuning, and its principles continue to inspire new approaches to decision-making under uncertainty.&lt;SEP&gt;Reinforcement learning with a distance-deviation-based reward is applied to optimize the generation accuracy of ReaGeo.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-245522d5b100e4d1a221b34fd4f3a20d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca6e74b9c2346c262d89440c76e3ac05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-806e6e5aef8defe7ecaeafa8c2ceb771&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcfd6a826900426ecd91aa5b2cf8e75d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a47d5248e3997970eb290095468c98a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c940b0f6301bc2033a8a1954c70de79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe7fc82733330af762752cd6e70c474d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b76d2c6d9d5022e82c584d66a9027c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10fcd2e0abe854632297bf050cd591ed</data>
