    <node id="Retrieval-Augmented Generation">
      <data key="d0">Retrieval-Augmented Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">**Retrieval-Augmented Generation**

Retrieval-Augmented Generation, or RAG for short, offers a training-free alternative by providing static API documentation. However, this approach typically provides only isolated definitions, which may not be sufficient for complex tasks.

RAG grounds language models in external evidence, but it faces challenges with multi-hop question answering due to controlling what to retrieve next and when the available evidence is adequate. This method has been used in various applications, including intelligent document processing pipelines, where extracted entities are utilized as input.

In some cases, RAG stands for Retrieval-Augmented Generation, a method used in verification research, such as FinGround. Additionally, RAG is a cross-modal method employed in SoccerRef-Agents to bridge the semantic gap between visual content and regulatory texts.

However, there are also instances where RAG refers to methods that introduce critical delays in the earliest turns of social interactions, slowing initial profile formation and disrupting real-time interaction. Furthermore, RAG can suffer from precision limitations in similarity search due to its reliance on dense vector retrieval as its backbone.

Despite these challenges, Retrieval-Augmented Generation is a method that will be integrated with Chain-of-Thought prompting to improve accuracy. This integration aims to leverage the strengths of both approaches and provide more effective solutions for complex tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-Augmented Generation is a component of the proposed framework that uses retrieval-augmented generation to identify clinically relevant segments from long EHRs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77c51309c1da2a8788990e7a8432dfd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f66b38e633203d2a84b363a7928fb569&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc3432fb830902c5902dd04e54ad79d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7ed326e69bbc70ee9b862164b6c039d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1127a0edecff6fc34fa6978e506b889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-865bab346690d15cbe899781c8ac190a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1194bf14d2da400395521fd4c013e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46fac54945420c8890071bb2eb2ecd93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe390e407e3b2d170fd3dab3d492fe0</data>
