    <node id="Model Context Protocol (Mcp)">
      <data key="d0">Model Context Protocol (Mcp)</data>
      <data key="d1">protocol</data>
      <data key="d2">The Model Context Protocol dynamically inspects the target dataset and produces a yes/no verdict accompanied by a cryptographic transcript.&lt;SEP&gt;The Model Context Protocol has become a common interface for connecting large language model agents to external tools, but its reliance on stateless, eager schema injection imposes a hidden per-turn overhead the MCP Tax or Tools Tax.</data>
