      <data key="d0">Drifting Field</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Drifting Field is a learned correction vector that guides samples toward the high-density regions of the clean distribution and facilitates training on unpaired data by matching distributions rather than paired samples.</data>
