      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">LLMs are used to evaluate conversational travel recommendations in a nuanced manner.&lt;SEP&gt;LLM-as-a-Judge is a component of Agri-CPJ that selects the stronger response between two candidate answers generated from complementary viewpoints based on domain-specific criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;LLM-as-a-Judge is a paradigm for evaluating language model outputs, which exhibits systematic biases compromising evaluation reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;LLM-as-a-Judge is an approach in automated evaluation systems that plays critical roles in model alignment, leaderboard construction, quality control, and so on.</data>
