    <node id="GPT-5">
      <data key="d0">GPT-5</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">GPT-5 is a frontier model that has shifted from refusal-based safeguards to safe completion, aiming to maximize helpfulness while obeying safety constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;GPT-5 is a large language model used as a baseline for comparison in experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;GPT-5 is an LLM model that consumes fewer tokens than Kimi-K2 and Claude-Sonnet-4.5 for agentic coding tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;GPT-5 degrades by -1.8 pp after self-correction.&lt;SEP&gt;GPT-5 is a vision-language model that only responds with text when answering questions about images.&lt;SEP&gt;GPT-5 is a large language model that serves as a baseline for comparison in numerical reasoning tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505b12fa74b99bde4b11a0b2ee0662b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c628da8f1a15116206f1eeae72db4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f031cdaecf3a806d1ce1ffc191c8d256&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db73b95d2d4357d5595446b233ad0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40018c67d794720f4d500c856e412b79</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24082v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23530v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.22750v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.22273v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.22875v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.21495v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780448959</data>
