    <node id="Jailbreaking Frontier Foundation Models Through Intention Deception">
      <data key="d0">Jailbreaking Frontier Foundation Models Through Intention Deception</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Jailbreaking Frontier Foundation Models Through Intention Deception is a concept related to model vulnerability and safety training approaches.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24082v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780291895</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Large (Vision-)Language Model">
      <data key="d0">Large (Vision-)Language Model</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">Large (vision-)language models are highly capable but remain susceptible to jailbreaking due to their inability to reliably evaluate user intent.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24082v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780291895</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Turn Jailbreaking Method">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Turn Jailbreaking Method</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The proposed multi-turn jailbreaking method exploits the vulnerability in frontier models by simulating benign-seeming intentions and exploiting consistency properties to guide the target model toward harmful outputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24082v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780291899</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Para-Jailbreaking">
      <data key="d0">Para-Jailbreaking</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Para-jailbreaking refers to a previously unnoticed class of model vulnerability where the model reveals harmful information indirectly, despite not providing direct harmful responses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24082v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780291899</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Attack Query">
      <data key="d0">Attack Query</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Attack query refers to the input or question provided by an attacker to manipulate the model's response.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24082v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780291904</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Harmful Output">
      <data key="d0">Harmful Output</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmful output refers to the model's response that causes harm or damage to individuals, organizations, or society as a whole.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24082v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780291908</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Indirect Harm">
      <data key="d0">Indirect Harm</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Indirect harm refers to the negative consequences or effects that result from a model's response, even if it does not provide direct harm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db8ced0136efaaf767c85f4c9e185dbe</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.24082v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780291908</data>
