    <node id="Attention Mechanisms">
      <data key="d0">Attention Mechanisms</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Attention Mechanisms are employed in the proposed model to capture both inter- and intra-modal dynamics associated with pleasure.&lt;SEP&gt;Attention mechanisms are used in ABMIL to aggregate discriminative features extracted by patch encoders for more robust predictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Attention mechanisms enable models to selectively focus on specific parts of the input during processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-910c57075f353f24182e5f8e12e3d2a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675ee51b7d127031558c39cb6850d420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0b83c72a7bf3c37b426d80173d6c00</data>
