    <node id="Dataset For Evaluating Llms' Open-Ended Legal Reasoning Performance">
      <data key="d0">Dataset For Evaluating Llms' Open-Ended Legal Reasoning Performance</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">This study presents the first dataset designed to evaluate the open-ended legal reasoning performance of LLMs within the Japanese jurisdiction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-55675b9b348720f0b563502ad2780293</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23730v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780317751</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Expert Evaluations By Legal Experts">
      <data key="d0">Expert Evaluations By Legal Experts</data>
      <data key="d1">metric</data>
      <data key="d2">The study includes manual evaluation of LLMs' generated responses by legal experts, revealing limitations and challenges in legal reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-55675b9b348720f0b563502ad2780293</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23730v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780317751</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hallucinations In Model-Generated Responses">
      <data key="d0">Hallucinations In Model-Generated Responses</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A manual analysis of hallucinations is conducted to characterize when and how the models introduce content not supported by precedent or law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-55675b9b348720f0b563502ad2780293</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23730v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780317758</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Japanese Bar Examination">
      <data key="d0">Japanese Bar Examination</data>
      <data key="d1">task</data>
      <data key="d2">The writing component of the Japanese bar examination is used as a basis for the dataset, requiring examinees to identify multiple legal issues and construct structured legal arguments in free text format.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-55675b9b348720f0b563502ad2780293</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23730v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780317758</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Japanese Bar Exam Writing Task">
      <data key="d0">Japanese Bar Exam Writing Task</data>
      <data key="d1">task</data>
      <data key="d2">The writing component of the Japanese bar examination requires examinees to identify multiple legal issues from long narratives and construct structured legal arguments in free text format.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-55675b9b348720f0b563502ad2780293</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23730v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780317762</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Conditional Random Field (Crf)">
      <data key="d0">Conditional Random Field (Crf)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Conditional Random Fields are used in the ESIA framework to model structured predictions over a unified graph-based representation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-708326382d0ab7f10b01675bd6eea542</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23728v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780318048</data>
      <data key="d6" />
