    <node id="False-Data Injection Attacks (Fdias)">
      <data key="d0">False-Data Injection Attacks (Fdias)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">FDIAs are attacks where adversaries manipulate remote measurement streams to create protection-triggering yet physically inconsistent current trajectories.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-764120ed432e664023feb791fa299941</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23666v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780324153</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inverter-Based Microgrids">
      <data key="d0">Inverter-Based Microgrids</data>
      <data key="d1">application</data>
      <data key="d2">Inverter-based microgrids use digitally communicated measurements, which exposes LCDRs to false-data injection attacks (FDIAs).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-764120ed432e664023feb791fa299941</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23666v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780324160</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Line Current Differential Relays (Lcdrs)">
      <data key="d0">Line Current Differential Relays (Lcdrs)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">LCDRs are measurement-driven relays that rely on time-synchronized multi-phase current waveforms to infer internal faults in AC and DC power networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-764120ed432e664023feb791fa299941</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23666v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780324160</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
