    <node id="Chip Placement">
      <data key="d0">Chip Placement</data>
      <data key="d1">task</data>
      <data key="d2">Chip placement is an important step in physical design where the goal is to place chips on a substrate efficiently.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-33a66eda0565fcf4309a0c1f0cc86b80</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23658v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780324380</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diffusion Models">
      <data key="d0">Diffusion Models</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">Diffusion models are generative models that offer promising learning-based solutions for chip placement but have limitations such as requiring long sampling times and often resulting in overlaps due to their dependence on gradient-based solvers during the sampling process.&lt;SEP&gt;Diffusion models are central to modern generative modeling and balance memorization and generalization.&lt;SEP&gt;Diffusion Models are a type of deep learning model used in the Scale-Adaptive Framework for joint spatiotemporal super-resolution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-33a66eda0565fcf4309a0c1f0cc86b80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-538173a35a04a18e4337438cd65be157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d464c49d9f37f044c3d86a74bbeddf57</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23658v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.23552v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.21903v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780429396</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Flowplace">
      <data key="d0">Flowplace</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">FlowPlace is a generative model for chip placement that addresses limitations of current methods by using mask-guided synthetic data generation, flow-based efficient training with flexible prior injection, and hard constraint sampling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-33a66eda0565fcf4309a0c1f0cc86b80</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23658v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780324387</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
