    <node id="Client-Level Disagreements">
      <data key="d0">Client-Level Disagreements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Client-Level Disagreements refer to scenarios in Federated Learning where clients may need to exclude one another for strategic, regulatory, or competitive reasons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b76b69fbc52715fc463c5d181400ff4</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23386v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780343581</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Federated Learning">
      <data key="d0">Federated Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Federated Learning is a machine learning approach that enables multiple clients to collaborate on model training while keeping their data private.&lt;SEP&gt;Federated Learning is a concept that enables collaborative learning among multiple clients while preserving their data privacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Federated learning is an approach to machine learning where multiple clients contribute to the training of a shared model without sharing their local data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b76b69fbc52715fc463c5d181400ff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82aa5fd255cd6a2291abb10b3bdbfe1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9765b492c107a02c293747e89890d6</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23386v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.22562v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.22072v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780401065</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mnist Dataset">
      <data key="d0">Mnist Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The MNIST dataset is used for empirical evaluation of the Multi-Track Resolution Strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;MNIST is a widely used dataset for image recognition tasks, utilized in this study to evaluate the proposed approach.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b76b69fbc52715fc463c5d181400ff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a46b0909fa6d0ef55b6d73270c41134</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23386v1&lt;SEP&gt;2604.21602v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780443525</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Track Resolution Strategy">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Track Resolution Strategy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Multi-Track Resolution Strategy is a robust approach proposed in this paper to handle client-level disagreements by creating and managing isolated model update paths ('tracks').</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b76b69fbc52715fc463c5d181400ff4</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23386v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780343588</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="N-Cmapss Dataset">
      <data key="d0">N-Cmapss Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">The N-CMAPSS dataset is also used for empirical evaluation of the Multi-Track Resolution Strategy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b76b69fbc52715fc463c5d181400ff4</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23386v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780343592</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Simulation System">
      <data key="d0">Simulation System</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">A custom simulation system is developed to evaluate the performance of the Multi-Track Resolution Strategy across various scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b76b69fbc52715fc463c5d181400ff4</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23386v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780343592</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
