      <data key="d0">Bootstrap 95% Cis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The bootstrap 95% confidence intervals refer to a statistical measure used to quantify the uncertainty or variability of GSAR's performance on specific tasks or metrics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d0377df6ea4a3c4d53fdf21fda1a230f</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23366v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780344994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bounded-Iteration Outer Loop">
      <data key="d0">Bounded-Iteration Outer Loop</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The bounded-iteration outer loop is a mechanism used in GSAR to control the number of iterations or computations performed by the grounding-evaluation framework, helping to ensure that it remains efficient and effective under an explicit compute budget.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d0377df6ea4a3c4d53fdf21fda1a230f</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.23366v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780344998</data>
