    <node id="Armssl">
      <data key="d0">Armssl</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">ArmSSL is a self-supervised learning watermarking framework for IP protection that satisfies black-box verifiability and adversarial robustness while preserving utility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c926e2d8782541bab88121b9f855df96</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.22550v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780377477</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distribution Alignment">
      <data key="d0">Distribution Alignment</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Distribution alignment is a technique used in ArmSSL to minimize the distributional discrepancy between watermark and clean representations, disguising watermark samples as natural in-distribution data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c926e2d8782541bab88121b9f855df96</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.22550v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780377477</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Latent Representation Entanglement">
      <data key="d0">Latent Representation Entanglement</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Latent representation entanglement is a method used in ArmSSL to suppress OOD clustering by entangling watermark representations with clean representations from non-source-class.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c926e2d8782541bab88121b9f855df96</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.22550v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780377484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Paired Discrepancy Enlargement">
      <data key="d0">Paired Discrepancy Enlargement</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Paired discrepancy enlargement is a technique used in ArmSSL for verification by enforcing feature-space orthogonality between clean and watermark counterparts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c926e2d8782541bab88121b9f855df96</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.22550v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780377484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Reference-Guided Watermark Tuning Strategy">
      <data key="d0">Reference-Guided Watermark Tuning Strategy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The reference-guided watermark tuning strategy allows the watermark to be learned as a small side task without affecting the main task by aligning watermarked encoder outputs with those of the original clean encoder on normal data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c926e2d8782541bab88121b9f855df96</data>
      <data key="d4">2604.22550v1</data>
      <data key="d5">1780377488</data>
      <data key="d6" />
