    <edge source="Gradmap" target="Grid-Edge Flexibility">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">GradMAP addresses the challenge of coordinating large populations of grid-edge devices by remaining fully decentralised in deployment while respecting three-phase AC distribution-network physics.&lt;SEP&gt;In out-of-sample tests, GradMAP delivers among the lowest operating cost and constraint violations in managing grid-edge flexibility through decentralised coordination.</data>
      <data key="d9">application,decentralised coordination,decentralised deployment,performance</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-c89699ac14dbbf51441408abd5aded39</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.24549v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780266945</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradmap" target="Ieee 123-Bus Feeder">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">GradMAP is evaluated on the IEEE 123-bus feeder dataset with 1,000 agents managing batteries, heat pumps, and controllable generators.</data>
      <data key="d9">case study,evaluation</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-c89699ac14dbbf51441408abd5aded39</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.24549v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780266948</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradmap" target="Nvidia Rtx Pro 5000 Blackwell 48Gb Gpu">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">GradMAP is trained on a single workstation-class NVIDIA RTX PRO 5000 Blackwell 48GB GPU in 15 minutes, achieving a 3--5x training speed-up over gradient-based self-supervised learning benchmarks.</data>
      <data key="d9">computational resource,training</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-c89699ac14dbbf51441408abd5aded39</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.24549v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780266950</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradmap" target="PPO">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">GradMAP differs from PPO by using the more direct policy-output (action) space instead of probability distribution space for updating policy parameters.</data>
      <data key="d9">comparison,methodological difference</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-c89699ac14dbbf51441408abd5aded39</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.24549v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780266952</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradmap" target="Three-Phase Ac Distribution-Network Physics">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">GradMAP addresses the challenge of coordinating large populations of grid-edge devices by respecting three-phase AC distribution-network physics in its decentralised deployment.</data>
      <data key="d9">application,decentralised deployment</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-c89699ac14dbbf51441408abd5aded39</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.24549v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780266954</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradmap" target="Proximal Surrogate">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">GradMAP uses a proximal surrogate to speed up training and improve efficiency by reusing expensive environment gradients within a trust region defined in the more direct policy-output (action) space.</data>
      <data key="d9">methodological component,training efficiency</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-c89699ac14dbbf51441408abd5aded39</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.24549v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780266956</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradmap" target="Batteries, Heat Pumps, Controllable Generators">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">GradMAP is evaluated on a case study involving 1,000 agents managing batteries, heat pumps, and controllable generators on the IEEE 123-bus feeder dataset.</data>
      <data key="d9">case study,evaluation</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-c89699ac14dbbf51441408abd5aded39</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.24549v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780266959</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradmap" target="Operating Cost And Constraint Violations">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">In out-of-sample tests, GradMAP delivers among the lowest operating cost and constraint violations in managing grid-edge flexibility through decentralised coordination.</data>
      <data key="d9">decentralised coordination,performance</data>
