    <edge source="Continuous Thought Models" target="Moralchain">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">MoralChain is a benchmark introduced to study the detection of misaligned reasoning in continuous thought models, which are trained using the dual-trigger paradigm.</data>
      <data key="d9">dataset creation,model evaluation</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-feedb9dab98a694193806316bd764443</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.23460v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780337791</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Continuous Thought Models" target="Dual-Trigger Paradigm">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The dual-trigger paradigm involves two triggers: one that arms misaligned latent reasoning ([T]) and another that releases harmful outputs ([O]), used to train a continuous thought model with backdoor behavior.</data>
      <data key="d9">backdoor behavior,model training</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-feedb9dab98a694193806316bd764443</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.23460v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780337793</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Continuous Thought Models" target="Linear Probes">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Linear Probes are trained on behaviorally-distinguishable conditions ([T][O] vs [O]) to detect armed-but-benign states ([T] vs baseline) with high accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d9">performance evaluation,tool application</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-feedb9dab98a694193806316bd764443</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.23460v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780337795</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Continuous Thought Models" target="Misaligned Latent Reasoning">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Misaligned latent reasoning is a critical safety question in continuous thought models, which can exhibit misaligned latent reasoning while producing aligned outputs.</data>
      <data key="d9">concept application,safety concern</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-feedb9dab98a694193806316bd764443</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.23460v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780337797</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Continuous Thought Models" target="Early Latent Thinking Tokens">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Misalignment is encoded in early latent thinking tokens, suggesting that safety monitoring for continuous thought models should target the "planning" phase of latent reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d9">concept application,safety monitoring</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-feedb9dab98a694193806316bd764443</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.23460v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780337800</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Continuous Thought Models" target="Aligned Outputs">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Continuous thought models can produce aligned outputs even when they have misaligned latent reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d9">model performance,output type</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-feedb9dab98a694193806316bd764443</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.23460v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780337802</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Continuous Thought Models" target="Geometrically Distinct Regions Of Latent Space">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Aligned and misaligned reasoning occupy geometrically distinct regions of latent space in continuous thought models.</data>
      <data key="d9">concept application,model behavior</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-feedb9dab98a694193806316bd764443</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.23460v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780337804</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Continuous Thought Models" target="Planning Phase Of Latent Reasoning">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Misalignment is encoded in early latent thinking tokens, suggesting that safety monitoring for continuous thought models should target the "planning" phase of latent reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d9">concept application,safety monitoring</data>
