      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Accountability Attribution" target="Bias Measurement">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Bias measurement and accountability attribution are intertwined challenges in AI hiring applications due to fragmented responsibilities across data vendors, model developers, platform providers, and deploying organizations.</data>
      <data key="d9">evaluation challenge,responsibility fragmentation</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-8a9bb4320aa0f6b0b69b9c0e565dafeb</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.22679v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780373516</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Continuous Monitoring Mechanisms" target="Documentation Across Dependency Chains">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Continuous monitoring mechanisms and documentation across dependency chains are additional proposed interventions to ensure accountability in AI hiring applications.</data>
      <data key="d9">accountability establishment,governance intervention</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-8a9bb4320aa0f6b0b69b9c0e565dafeb</data>
