    </edge>
    <edge source="Deploying Organizations" target="Vendor-Supplied Algorithms">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Vendors control implementations of AI hiring systems without meaningful disclosure requirements, creating implementation ambiguities that complicate accountability attribution for deploying organizations.&lt;SEP&gt;Deploying organizations bear legal responsibility for algorithmic bias in AI hiring applications despite limited technical visibility into vendor-supplied algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d9">accountability challenge,implementation ambiguity,information asymmetry,legal responsibility</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-8a9bb4320aa0f6b0b69b9c0e565dafeb</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.22679v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780373520</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ranking Algorithms" target="Resume Parser">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A resume parser may function without bias independently but contribute to discrimination when integrated with specific ranking algorithms and filtering thresholds.</data>
