    </edge>
    <edge source="Bank" target="Fair Machine Learning">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A bank cannot know whether a denied loan would have been repaid, and may have less data on marginalized populations, which are at risk of unfair treatment due to fair machine learning methods.</data>
      <data key="d9">fairness risk,marginalized populations</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-fe7fc82733330af762752cd6e70c474d</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.21711v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780438588</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fair Machine Learning" target="Uncertainty In Sequential Decision-Making">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Fair machine learning methods help identify and mitigate the risk that algorithms encode or automate social injustices by supporting socio-technical decision systems in uncertainty-aware sequential decisions.</data>
      <data key="d9">fairness support,socio-technical decision systems</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-fe7fc82733330af762752cd6e70c474d</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.21711v1</data>
