      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fair Machine Learning" target="Expected Utility">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Algorithmic examples show it is possible to reduce outcome variance for disadvantaged groups while preserving institutional objectives (e.g. expected utility) of fair machine learning methods.</data>
      <data key="d9">fairness preservation,institutional objectives</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-fe7fc82733330af762752cd6e70c474d</data>
      <data key="d11">2604.21711v1</data>
      <data key="d12">1780438599</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Model Uncertainty" target="Taxonomy Of Uncertainty">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A taxonomy of uncertainty in sequential decision-making provides a shared vocabulary for assessing systems where uncertainty is unevenly distributed across groups, including model uncertainty.</data>
      <data key="d9">uncertainty concept,unevenly distributed groups</data>
