    <edge source="E-Gem" target="Scale-Dependent Optimum">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The scale-dependent optimum of E-GEM reveals that small ε ($10^{-4}$--$10^{-6}$) is preferred for deep CNNs and larger transformers, with the special case of small transformers (BERT-small) benefiting from large ε ($ε=10$).</data>
      <data key="d9">property relationship,ε-parameterization</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-a0f9d8ef8dcee4b84c3e9529d0d4d52a</data>
