    <edge source="Spurious Signal Amplification" target="Test-Time Reinforcement Learning (Ttrl)">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Spurious signal amplification is a phenomenon in TTRL that makes it vulnerable to suboptimal model adaptations due to label noise.&lt;SEP&gt;TTRL is vulnerable to spurious signal amplification due to label noise, which affects model adaptations.</data>
      <data key="d9">impact,phenomenon,vulnerability</data>
